## Before any build is executed, in this order

1. **The type sweep, before any typeface is named.** Every typography source in the library is
   walked in a fixed order and the record has to pass its gate. Kind of type first, exact face second.
   `python3 ~/claude-global-config/scripts/type-sweep.py init "<build dir>" --project <name> --niche <niche>`
   `node ~/claude-global-config/scripts/verify-type-sweep.mjs "<build dir>/type-sweep.json"`
   A venture whose face Jordan already approved is declared with `init --locked` and is never reopened.
2. **The mood board, before any code.** No page, deck, app or HTML deliverable gets written until
   a mood board exists and Jordan has seen it. Palette options, anchor candidates, motif, ground.
   Every face on it comes from the sweep in step 1.
   `python3 ~/claude-global-config/scripts/moodboard.py <file.html> --industry <category>`
   A document-shaped piece with no visual direction declares `MOODBOARD: n/a` in the file. Silence is not allowed.
3. **Jordan picks the typeface.** On a new identity the headline anchor is the one routine decision
   that is **not yours**. Shortlist with rendered samples and let him choose. Never pick and proceed.
4. **Name the tier.** CONVERSION (a form, booking, checkout, dashboard, scorecard) is lean and
   fast. SHOWPIECE (cinematic, flagship, hero, pitch, portfolio, award) gets a real motion engine,
   large type and depth. Shipping the lean ruleset when he asked for cinematic is the failure.
5. **Measure footage before designing a hero around it.**
   `python3 ~/claude-global-config/scripts/hero-fit.py <clip-or-photo>`
6. **Tokens before components.** Type scale, palette, spacing, grid. Then build.

